course: dictionary
lesson: 3852
title: Founding and the start of things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Founding means starting or creating something, like a city, a school or a club. It comes from the word found, which means to start. «Rome's legendary founding in 753 BC came 709 years before Julius Caesar was killed.» The years tell you when Rome began, so founding must mean the start of the city.
explain: Context clues help you check. «Kyiv's traditional founding date is AD 482» means the date when Kyiv is said to have started. Try the swap test: put "starting" in place of founding and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so your meaning is right.
explain: Founding can also be an adjective, describing someone who was there at the beginning. A founding member of a club is one of its first members. «New Zealand's founding document» is the important paper from the time the country began. The Treaty of Waitangi was signed in 1840, and the clue is in the word founding.
fact: Founding means starting or creating something new, such as a city, school, company or group.
fact: Found is the verb meaning to start, so founding is the -ing form of found.
fact: «Founding fathers» are the people who started a country, especially the USA.
fact: «A founding member» means one of the first members of a club or group.
fact: Dates in BC count backwards towards year 1, so 753 BC is much older than 44 BC.
exercise: «Rome's legendary founding in 753 BC came 709 years before Julius Caesar was killed.» What does founding mean here? | The painting of the city walls | The end of a long war | * The start of the city | The closing of the city
exercise: Ella says, «She is a founding member of the club.» What does founding member mean? | The newest member who joined last week | A member who is always late | A member who has left the club | * One of the first members
exercise: «Kyiv's traditional founding date is AD 482, which makes it 1,544 years old in 2026.» Find and copy one word that means the start of something. | old | * founding | years | traditional
test: «The Treaty of Waitangi, signed in 1840, is New Zealand's founding document.» What does founding document suggest? | A document written last week | A document about the weather | A document that is very short | * A document from when the country began
test: Max says, «The founding of our school was a long time ago.» What is the best meaning of founding here? | * The time when the school was started | The time when the school was full of children | The time when the school closed | The time when the school was painted
exam: Lily says founding means the same as found, so it is a noun. Is she right? | * Yes, found and founding are the same word type | No, founding is always an adjective and never a noun | No, founding can be a noun or an adjective, and found is the verb meaning to start | Yes, and both mean very old
